  "evidence": "From A: Freeze non-essential immigration; stop the boats; swift detention/deportation; leave the ECHR; patriotic curriculum and British identity pledges; 40,000 more police with zero‑tolerance and tougher sentencing; scrap Net Zero; scrap the Equalities Act’s DE&I regime; NHS pledges (zero waiting lists, tax relief for private care, vouchers). From B: Right to see a GP in seven days with 8,000 more GPs; urgent NHS dentistry; mental health hubs and school professionals; free personal care and a Carer’s Minimum Wage; Net zero by 2045, Clean Air Act, end sewage scandal; build 380,000 homes incl. 150,000 social, ban no‑fault evictions, three‑year tenancies; defend the Human Rights Act, ban conversion therapy, make misogyny a hate crime, strengthen disability rights; end the Hostile Environment and create safe legal routes; progressive tax reforms and skills/apprenticeship support.",
  "reasoning": "The profile prioritises Care and Equality most, with Proportionality next and only moderate weight on Loyalty and Authority. B foregrounds care (NHS, social care, mental health, housing, clean air/water) and equality/rights protections, while A leans heavily on loyalty/authority (borders, policing, patriotic curriculum) and rolls back DE&I and Net Zero, making B the closer match despite A’s NHS pledges.",
